Sval: a page in an agent's tab opens its tabs, and saves its PDFs, as the agent's

A tab a page in an agent's tab asks for, by target=_blank or window.open, and
one the user opens from a link there, by a middle or modified click or the
context menu, open in the background of the agent's own window, whichever
window the page is in. PDF.js's Save in an agent's tab is the agent's
download. BrowserDOMWindow.createContentWindowInFrame,
URILoadingHelper.openLinkIn and PdfjsParent._saveURL ask SvalAgentRouting
first, which answers for the agents an open gate holds, and go on as Firefox
does for every other tab.

Firefox opens a page's new tab in the opener's window, selected, and from a
popup in the frontmost full window; PdfjsParent saves with no browsing
context on its transfer, so the download guard cannot tell whose save it is.
No chrome API changes where a tab opens or decides that save.

